From 182c35e69884bf988a4cca8abda5579ef602742c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Jonat=C3=A3=20Bolzan=20Loss?= <jonata@jonata.org>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 23:41:07 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 07/29] Haiku: base/ process and system info, PartitionAlloc
 threads

base/ gets Haiku versions of the four per-OS files the BSDs have (process
handle, iterator, metrics, sys_info), built on team_info, area_info,
team_usage_info and system_info; libkvm/epoll-shim are not linked.
PartitionAlloc: thread ids from find_thread, stack top from
get_thread_info, no sys/syscall.h. The export-template self-tests skip
__declspec on Haiku (its GCC maps __declspec to __attribute__). ANGLE
gets its null backend, its only one on Haiku.
